# Shadows /usr/share/applications/avahi-discover.desktop.
#
# $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications outranks /usr/share/applications for the same
# desktop-file ID, and the spec defines Hidden=true as "strictly equivalent to
# the .desktop file not existing at all". So this deletes the launcher entry
# without touching the avahi package — which cannot be removed at all: it is a
# HARD dependency of cups, libcups (-> gtk3 -> blueman, nemo, discord, obsidian,
# chrome …) and pipewire-pulse, which links libavahi-client.so directly.
#
# NoDisplay is set as well as Hidden purely for launchers that honour only the
# former; either one alone would do the job in a spec-compliant one.
#
# This entry could not start even if you wanted it: /usr/bin/avahi-discover is a
# python script that imports dbus, and python-dbus is not installed here (it is
# an optdepend of avahi that nothing pulled in). The terminal equivalent, which
# does work once avahi-daemon is running, is:  avahi-browse -a -r
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Avahi Zeroconf Browser
NoDisplay=true
Hidden=true
